# Why count?
# Because we do not want to copy and paste subnet resources four times.
# This:
# count = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)
# means:
# Create one public subnet for each CIDR in public_subnet_cidrs
# Since you have:
# ["10.0.1.0/24", "10.0.2.0/24"]
# Terraform creates 2 public subnets.
# Why count.index?
# It selects the matching CIDR and AZ.
# Example:
# count.index = 0
# CIDR = 10.0.1.0/24
# AZ   = eu-west-1a
# count.index = 1
# CIDR = 10.0.2.0/24
# AZ   = eu-west-1b
# Now run:
# terraform fmt -recursive
# terraform validate
# terraform plan
# terraform state list (it is used to see get state list)

// so we have covered 

